# Minimize the build context for our Dockerfiles.
#
# Two Dockerfiles share this worktree as their build root:
#   * `docker/openclaw-with-plugin.Dockerfile` needs `gateway_plugin/` only.
#   * `docker/gateway.Dockerfile` needs `clawsocialarena/` + `pyproject.toml`.
#
# We exclude the broad buckets first, then explicitly un-exclude the
# paths the gateway image needs (see the `!` re-inclusions below). This
# keeps the build context small while giving both images the files
# they actually read.

# Node/TypeScript build artifacts.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/.next

# Python virtualenvs, caches, build output.
**/.venv
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/*.egg-info
**/build
**/htmlcov
**/.coverage
**/test_output

# Version control and worktree scaffolding.
.git
.gitattributes
.worktrees
worktree

# Arena docs, paper drafts, and external knowledge drops.
docs
neurips
knowledge
benchmark
results
fixtures

# Python pieces the openclaw image does not need. The gateway image
# DOES need `clawsocialarena/` and `pyproject.toml`, so those are
# re-included below.
clawsocialarena
tests
scripts
pyproject.toml
*.py
*.sqlite
*.db

# Re-include what `docker/gateway.Dockerfile` reads. The openclaw
# Dockerfile does not `COPY` these, so their presence in the context is
# harmless there.
!clawsocialarena
!clawsocialarena/**
!pyproject.toml

# Editor / local state.
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
.env*
!.env.example

# Skill / agent config scaffolding.
.agent-config
.claude
agents
knowledge
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
AGENTS.local.md

# Docker auxiliary files (the Dockerfile is selected with -f; we do not
# need the full `docker/` tree inside the image context).
docker/*
!docker/openclaw-with-plugin.Dockerfile
!docker/gateway.Dockerfile
!docker/agent-entrypoint.sh
!docker/compose-templates
!docker/compose-templates/**
